\@writefile{tdo}{\contentsline {todo}{\fcolorbox {black}{green}{\textcolor {green}{o}}\ Note that this validation only works in the case of a rigid interface - naturally the film will shape as the droplet falls, preventing $\ell $ from reaching 0. Something something scaling, $\ell $ has a natural lower bound of $\mathcal  {O}(\text  {St}^{-1/3})$, or the neck length $\ell _\text  {neck}$, whichever is smaller. Hence, as long as we enforce $\Delta r \ll \text  {St}^{-1/3}$ (in our simulation, we use $\Delta r = 0.05 \min \{\text  {ahh}\}$), we get the behaviour as above.}{13}{section*.59}\protected@file@percent }
